<title>SWITZERLAND: Lindt says profits rising more than sales.</title>
<headline>Lindt says profits rising more than sales.</headline>
<dateline>KILCHBERG, Switzerland 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chocolate and confectionery maker Lindt &amp; Spruengli AG said 1996 figures should show profitability rising at a higher rate than sales.</p>
<p>Lindt earlier said consolidated sales climbed 5.8 percent last year from the year before to 973 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>&quot;For the year 1996 the group expects an increase in profitability that should surpass the one of consolidated sales,&quot; Lindt said in a statement. It did not elaborate except to say that detailed information would be given at a news conference on April 1.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
